---
// CitationDossier.astro - Feature 13: Think-Tank Citation Builder & Fact-Checking Vault
---
<div class="hud-panel hud-corner citation-card">
  <div class="cite-header">
    <div>
      <div class="cite-title-row">
        <span class="badge badge-pantone-2022">VERIFIED INTELLIGENCE</span>
        <h3 class="font-mono cite-heading">THINK-TANK CITATION & FACT-CHECKING DOSSIER</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="font-mono text-muted" style="font-size: 0.76rem;">Generate instant authoritative citations (CSIS, RUSI, ISW, IISS, CRS) formatted for YouTube descriptions & Substack.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Quick Format Switcher -->
    <div class="format-toggles font-mono">
      <button class="fmt-btn active" data-fmt="youtube">YouTube Description</button>
      <button class="fmt-btn" data-fmt="markdown">Substack Markdown</button>
      <button class="fmt-btn" data-fmt="chicago">Chicago Manual</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cite-grid">
    <!-- Think-Tank Preset Sources -->
    <div class="sources-list-box hud-panel font-mono">
      <div class="box-head">
        <span class="badge badge-pantone-2021">PRESET DEFENSE SOURCES</span>
        <span style="font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text-dim);">SELECT TO INSERT</span>
      </div>

      <div class="sources-stack">
        <div class="source-item" data-id="csis_missile">
          <div class="source-item-top">
            <span class="source-name" style="color: #BB2649;">CSIS Missile Defense Project</span>
            <span class="source-tag">Missiles / A2AD</span>
          </div>
          <p class="source-sub font-sans">"Missile Threat: CSIS Aerospace Security Project - Ballistic & Hypersonic Profiles"</p>
        </div>

        <div class="source-item" data-id="iiss_balance">
          <div class="source-item-top">
            <span class="source-name" style="color: #F5DF4D;">IISS The Military Balance 2024</span>
            <span class="source-tag">ORBAT / Fleet Tonnage</span>
          </div>
          <p class="source-sub font-sans">"International Institute for Strategic Studies: Annual Assessment of Global Military Capabilities"</p>
        </div>

        <div class="source-item" data-id="rusi_ew">
          <div class="source-item-top">
            <span class="source-name" style="color: #6667AB;">RUSI Defense Studies</span>
            <span class="source-tag">EW / Land Warfare</span>
          </div>
          <p class="source-sub font-sans">"Royal United Services Institute: Jamming the Kill Chain - Modern Electronic Warfare Analysis"</p>
        </div>

        <div class="source-item" data-id="crs_navy">
          <div class="source-item-top">
            <span class="source-name" style="color: #FFBE98;">Congressional Research Service (CRS)</span>
            <span class="source-tag">US Naval Procurement</span>
          </div>
          <p class="source-sub font-sans">"Navy Force Structure and Shipbuilding Plans: Background and Issues for Congress (RL32665)"</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Generated Citation Output Box -->
    <div class="citation-output-box hud-panel font-mono">
      <div class="box-head">
        <span class="badge badge-pantone-2024">GENERATED CITATION BLOCK</span>
        <button class="btn-tactical btn-outline" id="copyCitationBlockBtn" style="font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 0.25rem 0.55rem;">📋 Copy Block</button>
      </div>

      <pre class="citation-pre" id="citationOutputText">
=== SOURCES & RESEARCH DOSSIER ===
1. [CSIS Missile Defense Project] "Iskander-M (SS-26 Stone) Technical Profile", Center for Strategic and International Studies (2024). https://missilethreat.csis.org/missile/ss-26-2/
2. [IISS] "The Military Balance: Naval Surface & Subsurface Fleet Capacities", International Institute for Strategic Studies (London, 2024).
3. [CRS] "China Naval Modernization: Implications for U.S. Navy Capabilities", Congressional Research Service Report RL33153 (Updated 2024).
4. [SATELLITE IMAGERY] Commercial Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) imagery via Capella Space / European Space Agency Copernicus Sentinel-1.
      </pre>

      <div class="credibility-badge font-mono">
        <span class="cred-dot"></span>
        <span>PEER-REVIEWED DEFENSE THINK-TANK COMPLIANT</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script is:inline>
  const citations = {
    youtube: `=== SOURCES & INTEL DOSSIER (YOUTUBE DESCRIPTION) ===
1. [CSIS] "Missile Threat: Iskander-M & Hypersonic Glide Envelopes", Center for Strategic and International Studies. https://missilethreat.csis.org/
2. [IISS] "The Military Balance 2024: Global Naval Order of Battle", Routledge / International Institute for Strategic Studies.
3. [RUSI] "The Kill Web: Tactical Electronic Warfare and Counter-Stealth Radar", Royal United Services Institute.
4. [CRS] "U.S. Navy Carrier Strike Group Force Structure & Hypersonic Vulnerabilities", Congressional Research Service Report RL32665.
5. [IMAGERY] Satellite verification via Planet Labs / ESA Copernicus Sentinel-2.`,

    markdown: `### Primary Defense Dossier Sources
- **CSIS Missile Defense Project**: *Iskander-M & Hypersonic Systems Technical Dossier*. [CSIS Aerospace Project](https://missilethreat.csis.org/).
- **IISS The Military Balance**: *Surface Fleet Tonnage & VLS Cell Allocations (2024 ed.)*. London: Routledge.
- **RUSI Defense Publications**: *Countering Precision Fires in Contested Archipelagos*. Royal United Services Institute.
- **Congressional Research Service**: *RL32665: Navy Force Structure and Shipbuilding Plans for Congress*.`,

    chicago: `1. Center for Strategic and International Studies. "Iskander-M (SS-26 Stone)." Missile Defense Project, 2024. https://missilethreat.csis.org/.
2. International Institute for Strategic Studies. The Military Balance 2024. London: Routledge, 2024.
3. Congressional Research Service. China Naval Modernization: Implications for U.S. Navy Capabilities. Report RL33153, 2024.
4. Royal United Services Institute. Modern Electronic Warfare and Radar Cross Section Signatures. RUSI Occasional Paper, 2024.`
  };

  document.querySelectorAll('.fmt-btn').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.querySelectorAll('.fmt-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
      btn.classList.add('active');
      const fmt = btn.getAttribute('data-fmt');
      document.getElementById('citationOutputText').innerText = citations[fmt] || citations.youtube;
    });
  });

  document.getElementById('copyCitationBlockBtn')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const text = document.getElementById('citationOutputText').innerText;
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
    const btn = document.getElementById('copyCitationBlockBtn');
    btn.innerText = '✓ Copied!';
    setTimeout(() => btn.innerText = '📋 Copy Block', 2000);
  });
</script>

<style>
  .citation-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .cite-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(147, 149, 151, 0.15);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .cite-title-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .cite-heading {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-main);
  }

  .format-toggles {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .fmt-btn {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .fmt-btn.active {
    background: var(--bg-card-hover);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .cite-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1.3fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .sources-list-box,
  .citation-output-box {
    background: rgba(14, 19, 26, 0.95);
    padding: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .box-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(147, 149, 151, 0.15);
  }

  .sources-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  .source-item {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(147, 149, 151, 0.12);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }
  .source-item:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
  }

  .source-item-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }

  .source-tag {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .source-sub {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .citation-pre {
    background: #080B0F;
    border: 1px solid rgba(147, 149, 151, 0.15);
    padding: 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-main);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border-radius: 3px;
    flex: 1;
  }

  .credibility-badge {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: #00FF88;
    background: rgba(0, 255, 136, 0.05);
    padding: 0.35rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 255, 136, 0.2);
  }

  .cred-dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #00FF88;
    box-shadow: 0 0 6px #00FF88;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .cite-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
